---
interface Props {
  section: 'philosophy' | 'status';
}

const { section } = Astro.props;
---

{section === 'philosophy' && (
  <section class="section philosophy-section" id="philosophy" aria-labelledby="philosophy-heading">
    <div class="shell editorial-layout">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">WHY TURBOJ EXISTS</p>
        <h2 class="section-heading" id="philosophy-heading">Good tools get out of your way.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <p class="body-copy">TurboJ started with a simple idea: editing, compiling, and running Java should feel immediate.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">That same focused interface now supports Maven projects, semantic navigation, refactoring, source formatting, and JUnit tests.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">The goal is not to reproduce every feature of a large IDE. It is to keep everyday Java development close to the code, with fewer interruptions.</p>
        <p class="section-closing">Old-school focus. Modern Java.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{section === 'status' && (
  <section class="section status-section" id="status" aria-labelledby="status-heading">
    <div class="shell editorial-layout">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">UNDER ACTIVE DEVELOPMENT</p>
        <h2 class="section-heading" id="status-heading">A working Java environment. Still evolving.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <p class="body-copy">TurboJ 1.0.10 is a macOS development preview with a native editor, Java intelligence, Maven support, refactoring, formatting, and JUnit testing.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">The application has been exercised on Apple Silicon. Public distribution and independent library releases are still being prepared.</p>
        <p class="body-copy">Source code, examples, and technical documentation are available on GitHub.</p>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="#demo">Back to the editor</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}
